  "_calibration_note": "REAL calibration for the 11 guild screenshots in .secrets/ocr-samples/ (D-09). One group per screenshot file — the common samples are arbitrary scrolled crops, so each has its own pixel map. Rects are pixel rectangles (top-left origin): x, y, w, h, targeting each stat row's VALUE area only (values are right-aligned per column; labels are never inside a rect). They were calibrated from Tesseract word bounding boxes over each sample (layout dump), padded ~8px horizontally / ~6px vertically. Region 'type' defaults to the numeric locale parse; 'text' (sampbasic header fields) compares case-insensitive strings and uses a letter whitelist. Categories drive the per-category accuracy report: 'basic' = character header screen (job, nickname, combat power — first screenshot of the capture flow), 'ideal' = optimal inputs, 'common' = real-world suboptimal inputs. To recalibrate after a game UI change: run `node scripts/ocr-spike.mjs --info` for resolutions and re-derive rects from a layout pass.",
